{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Then He saw and recounted it</b> — ויספרה is not from ויספר משה ('and Moses recounted'), but rather from מספר ('number/counting'), or from וללמדה ספר ('and to teach it a writing'). The meaning is that it is written/inscribed before Him. Similarly: יספר שחקים בחכמה ('He recounts the clouds with wisdom')."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads ויספרה as either 'counted it' (root ספר, counting) or 'inscribed it in a writing' (ספר, a document), both distinct from the hiphil 'recounted/told' as in Numbers 33:2. The clause העניין היא כתובה אצלו is rendered as 'it is written/inscribed before Him,' capturing the sense that Wisdom's matter is recorded in His possession."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:56.271076371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}